---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ImagePanel from '../components/ImagePanel.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Orivia: how an artisanal mining operation grew into an advisory practice across the full minerals supply chain in Sub-Saharan Africa."
>
  <section class="section intro-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal"><a href="/">&larr; Home</a></p>
      <h1 class="reveal">About Orivia</h1>
      <p class="lede reveal">
        Orivia started as a pioneering initiative in artisanal and
        small-scale mining (ASM). It has grown into something broader: an
        operator and advisor working across the full minerals supply
        chain, from artisanal to mid-size and large-scale, in frontier
        markets, with a particular focus on Sub-Saharan Africa.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ImagePanel
    src="/images/community-portrait.jpg"
    alt="Women from the mining community Orivia's operations are built around"
  >
    <h2 class="reveal">Where We Started</h2>
    <p class="reveal">
      Orivia began by operating its own artisanal and small-scale mining
      site, driven by a commitment to sustainability, ethics and
      responsible sourcing. Running that operation, day to day, taught us
      what the sector&rsquo;s standards actually require on the ground,
      beyond what appears on paper.
    </p>
  </ImagePanel>

  <section class="section grown-section">
    <div class="wrap grown-grid">
      <h2 class="reveal">A Mandate That Grew With the Sector</h2>
      <div class="reveal">
        <p>
          As our own operation matured, other parts of the sector started
          asking for the same rigour we apply to ourselves. That advisory
          side of Orivia has since grown to cover:
        </p>
        <ul class="grown-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Artisanal &amp; small-scale miners</strong> seeking a
            practical path toward formalisation and responsible sourcing
            readiness.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Large-scale mining and exploration companies</strong>
            operating alongside or acquiring ASM sites, or searching for
            land in the first place, who need to understand and manage
            that interface responsibly.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Project developers</strong> who need a full project
            proposal built, from land access through bringing local and
            international stakeholders to the same table.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Investors</strong> assessing capital deployment into
            ASM-adjacent projects and frontier-market mining assets.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Buyers and traders</strong>, including sourcing
            mandates in the gold and diamond trade, who need verifiable,
            defensible answers about where a mineral actually came from.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          All of it is grounded in Sub-Saharan Africa and other frontier
          markets, where the gap between informal practice and formal
          market expectations is widest, and where the advisory work
          matters most.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section stats-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="reveal">The Sector by the Numbers</h2>
      <p class="stats-intro reveal">
        ASM is often treated as a footnote to formal, large-scale mining.
        The numbers say otherwise. Figures below are the most widely
        cited estimates; ranges reflect genuine disagreement between
        sources.
      </p>
      <div class="stats-grid">
        <div class="stat reveal">
          <span class="stat-num">~45M</span>
          <p>
            people work directly in ASM across roughly 80 countries,
            the largest mining workforce of any kind (World Bank &amp;
            Pact, <em>2023 State of the ASM Sector</em>).
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat reveal">
          <span class="stat-num">$30B+</span>
          <p>
            estimated annual value of ASM gold output alone, before
            diamonds and other minerals are even counted (industry and
            academic estimates, early-to-mid 2020s).
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat reveal">
          <span class="stat-num">15&ndash;20%</span>
          <p>
            of global gold production and a similar share of global
            diamond production is estimated to come from ASM (World Gold
            Council; World Diamond Council; GIA).
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat reveal">
          <span class="stat-num">3,600+ t</span>
          <p>
            tonnes of gold mined worldwide in 2024, a record high. ASM
            accounts for a meaningful share of that total on its own
            (World Gold Council).
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="stats-note reveal">
        Mining statistics shift year to year and vary by source. Treat
        these as directional, and check current figures before quoting
        them externally.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta">
    <div class="wrap cta-inner reveal">
      <h2>Work With Orivia</h2>
      <p>
        Tell us where you sit in the value chain, and we&rsquo;ll tell you
        how we can help.
      </p>
      <a class="pill-btn" href="/contact">Connect</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 720px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .grown-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.6fr;
    gap: var(--gap);
  }

  .grown-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .grown-list li {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }

  .grown-list strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: "Fraunces", serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .stats-section {
    background: rgba(5, 40, 18, 0.04);
  }

  .stats-intro {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .stats-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .stat {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .stat-num {
    font-family: "Fraunces", serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    color: var(--ink);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .stat p {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .stats-note {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    opacity: 0.75;
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .cta {
    background: rgba(5, 40, 18, 0.05);
  }

  .cta-inner {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .cta-inner p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .grown-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .stats-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .stats-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
